=========================================================================
🚀 MODULE 3: HYPERLINKS, IMAGES AUR DEEP PATH ROUTING
=========================================================================
Description: Web pages ko aapas mein connect karna, Relative aur Absolute paths 
ka asli mechanical khel, aur Images ko structural tareeqe se manage karna.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. HYPERLINKS (<a> - Anchor Tag) - Web Pages Ko Jodna
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Anchor tag ka use website par links banane ke liye hota hai. Iska sabse main 
aur compulsory attribute hai 'href' (Hypertext Reference):

<a href="https://google.com" target="_blank" title="Google par jao">Google Kholein</a>

🛠️ ATTRIBUTE BREAKDOWN:
* href: Iske andar hum us target web page ya destination ka address (URL) 
  dalte hain jahan hume user ko bhejna hai.
* target="_blank": Agar aap yeh nahi likhoge, toh link usi chalte huyen tab 
  mein khul jayegi aur user aapki website se bahar chala jayega. target="_blank" 
  likhne se browser hamesha link ko ek Naye Tab (New Tab) mein kholta hai.
* title: Jab user is link ke upar apna mouse pointer le jata hai (hover karta hai), 
  toh ek chota sa helpful tooltip box dikhta hai jisme title ka text show hota hai.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. FILE PATHS: ABSOLUTE VS RELATIVE (Raste Ka Asli Khel)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Jab aap apni website mein koi photo lagate ho (<img>) ya koi doosra internal 
page jodte ho, toh computer engine ko rasta (path) do tarike se bataya jata hai:

* Absolute Path (Poora Address):
  Jab file aapke computer par nahi balki internet par kisi teesri website ya 
  server par padi ho. Isme poora protocol likhna padta hai.
  Example: href="https://example.com/assets/photo.jpg"

* Relative Path (Aapke Folders Ka Rasta):
  Yeh aapke project folder ke current structure ke hisab se chalta hai. Isme 3 
  main rules hote hain jo hamesha yaad rakhne hain:
  1. src="logo.png" ──> Iska matlab file usi SAME folder mein padi hai jahan 
     aapki HTML file hai.
  2. src="images/logo.png" ──> Iska matlab HTML file ke bilkul barabar mein ek 
     'images' naam ka folder hai, aur photo us folder ke andar rakhi hai.
  3. src="../logo.png" ──> Isme '../' ka matlab hota hai EK FOLDER BAHAR 
     (PEECHE) JAANA. Agar aapka HTML code kisi inner sub-folder ke andar band hai 
     aur photo usse ek step piche main directory mein hai, toh piche jaane ke 
     liye '../' lagate hain.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. IMAGES TAG (<img>) - Visual Media Architecture
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Website par photo dikhane ke liye hum <img> tag use karte hain. Yeh ek 
Self-closing ya Empty tag hai (yaani iska koi ending </img> companion nahi hota):

<img src="avatar.jpg" alt="Rahul Kumar ki Profile Photo" width="200" height="200">

🛠️ ATTRIBUTE BREAKDOWN:
* src (Source): Photo ka relative ya absolute file path.
* alt (Alternative Text) ──> SKI SAKHT ZAROORAT HAI! Iske do sabse bade fayde hain:
  1. Slow Internet / Broken Link: Agar user ka internet slow hai ya image delete 
     ho gayi hai, toh photo ki jagah yeh text dikhega taaki user ko pata chal sake 
     ki yahan kis cheez ki photo thi.
  2. Accessibility & SEO: Blind log jo screen reader software use karte hain, unka 
     software is alt text ko padh kar sunata hai. Google ka robot bhi photo ko dekh 
     nahi sakta, wo alt text se hi pehchanta hai ki photo kis baare mein hai.
* width aur height: Photo ka size pixel (px) mein fix karne ke liye.

